notes.content:
Hello friends, how are you doing?

For the past month I've been constantly trying to improve Burning Skies Arcade, with the help of your feedback, there where 2 big updates in this period, but since I didn't posted about the first one, I'm posting about both here. Here's what changed:

[b]Update 1.01[/b]

- Player Lifebar remade, to be less intrusive;
- Boss Lifebar remade, and now it shows the name of the boss;
- Fixed a bug that caused made players unable to change the body on the body select screen/
- Improved the way that enemies are spawned, so they are in a better position at the screen;
- Adjusted the boss intro;
- Fixed some menu itens, that displayed incorrectly; 
- Fixed issues with the steel mill boss, that made impossible to fight him;
- Adjusted some 'Destroy boss' challenges, that didn't had the path on the correct width;

[b]Update 1.02[/b]
- Fixed a bug that made the timer still running with the game paused on challenges;
- Fixed the challenges complete screen that where not showing;
- Added a reset all challenges on the challenges complete screen;
- Changed the behavior of the language select screen, now the players only need to select the language without needing to click on the "back" button (wich where not clear)
- Fixed the walls and floor foes being spawned in the middle of the screen;

Plus a bunch of smaller fixes I did and forgot to write down =S

I also released 3 DLCs for players who want to support the project, and also me as a game developer (I'm not funded by publishers and keep the lights on majoritarily with sales here from steam)

Here's a bundle with all of them and with an aditional 20% off
https://store.steampowered.com/bundle/42030/Burning_Skies_Arcade__Premium_Supporter_Bundle/

I also started [url=https://steamcommunity.com/app/2290190/discussions/0/4515505814160004254/]a feedback thread[/url] so if you want to share any feedback you can do it there or in our [url=https://discord.nukgames.com/]discord server[/url]

If you enjoyed the game, please leave a review it's very important for small games to beign noticed by the algorithm. 

Thank you for the support
Paulo.
